From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: retire only the expired bridge subflow

When a hardware subflow expires or its slot is reused, the bridge stats
walk must remove that subflow, not the parent L2 flow. Clearing the parent
removes it from the bridge lookup table and frees all its subflows,
including the next node saved by the ongoing safe iteration.

Clear cur after transferring its accounting to the parent. This retains
the bridge rule and the remaining subflows until tc removes the rule.

Signed-off-by: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>

---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
@@ -625,7 +625,7 @@ mtk_flow_entry_update_l2(struct mtk_ppe
 		if (!mtk_flow_entry_update(ppe, cur, packets, bytes)) {
 			entry->prev_packets += cur->prev_packets;
 			entry->prev_bytes += cur->prev_bytes;
-			__mtk_foe_entry_clear(ppe, entry, false);
+			__mtk_foe_entry_clear(ppe, cur, false);
 			continue;
 		}
 
